<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Transvaal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Transvaal is the region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> lying between the Vaal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a> rivers. Settled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a> from the 1830s, it formed the South African Republic, was annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> as the Transvaal Colony after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>, and became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal-province">Transvaal Province</a> of the Union of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in 1910. In 1994 it was divided into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauteng">Gauteng</a>, Limpopo, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpumalanga">Mpumalanga</a> and part of North West.</p></div>
